INTERPRETATION

The accepted bounded learned U-recruitment behavior has now transferred into
a four-stage compositional service without retraining or authority increase.

Task-4 had already been independently validated with the exact parent at the
same external one-request-per-epoch load.

On ten completely fresh paired worlds the learned recruiter caused 62 real
developmental recruitment differences while every pair preserved the
pre-registered functional envelope.

The learner remained blind to task identity, program identity, stage
identity, phase, lesion, absolute position, global queue, evaluator
correctness, and future information.

H and all committed-cell authorities remained exact teacher.

This extends the successful transfer lineage across:

Task-1;
two-stage Task-2;
three-stage Task-3;
four-stage Task-4.

BOUNDARY

Do not increase alpha.

Do not give learned authority to C/S.

Do not add online adaptation or recursive self-modification.

NEXT SCIENTIFIC QUESTION

Run one fresh independent Task-4 confirmation with unchanged authority,
weights, OBS-V1, load, repair maturity, lesion, and qualification bars.

Only after independent confirmation should the next task-distance experiment
decide whether to continue simple sequential depth or change compositional
structure.

PLAIN-SPEAK INTERPRETATION

The four-step transfer worked.

The same small neural recruiter that learned earlier in the lineage made real
cell-development decisions on a deeper four-stage job and the organism still
matched the hand-written parent across every required measure.

Ten out of ten fair comparisons passed.

No wrong answers.
No expired jobs.
No recovery penalty.
No extra neural authority.

The next test is a fresh second set of four-step worlds to make sure this
result repeats before we make the task structurally different.

